(4199648, 603787, 72769, '<td valign="top">This is the kind of photo that needs no caption, no explanation. It just grabs your attention and pulls emotion out of you.</td>', 'This is the kind of photo that needs no caption, no explanation. It just grabs your attention and pulls emotion out of you.', '2007-10-27 16:02:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199676, 602939, 208, '<td valign="top">Fantastic job with the depth of field on this one.</td>', 'Fantastic job with the depth of field on this one.', '2007-10-27 16:40:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199681, 602409, 208, '<td valign="top">Terrible title for this challenge, but a great shot.</td>', 'Terrible title for this challenge, but a great shot.', '2007-10-27 16:42:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199684, 602823, 208, '<td valign="top">It''s a shame your subject''s face is half-hidden. I think it would be better if he were either turned away like everyone else or facing the camera, either full-on or 3/4.</td>', 'It''s a shame your subject''s face is half-hidden. I think it would be better if he were either turned away like everyone else or facing the camera, either full-on or 3/4.', '2007-10-27 16:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199689, 604801, 208, '<td valign="top">I''m just not buying this as photojournalism. For that title, I''d expect to see more -- more leaves, a field of trees changing colors, a kid holding this leaf. If you''re going to do a set-up shot for photojournalism, there definitely needs to be more story.</td>', 'I''m just not buying this as photojournalism. For that title, I''d expect to see more -- more leaves, a field of trees changing colors, a kid holding this leaf. If you''re going to do a set-up shot for photojournalism, there definitely needs to be more story.', '2007-10-27 16:45:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199697, 604824, 208, '<td valign="top">That fluorescent lighting must have killed you. This looks like it might have been a set-up shot, though, so I would think you could have done something about the lights. Still, it''s a good shot for photojournalism. The bookbag next to the laptop is a nice touch.</td>', 'That fluorescent lighting must have killed you. This looks like it might have been a set-up shot, though, so I would think you could have done something about the lights. Still, it''s a good shot for photojournalism. The bookbag next to the laptop is a nice touch.', '2007-10-27 16:53:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199702, 604575, 208, '<td valign="top">Cool shot. But because it''s a photojournalism challenge, I need to see her face, especially with that title. Or (and I can''t believe I''m saying this) be more specific with the title. Ignoring the challenge though -- great job with the lighting; the backlight and hair halo are really nice as is the looooon shadow.</td>', 'Cool shot. But because it''s a photojournalism challenge, I need to see her face, especially with that title. Or (and I can''t believe I''m saying this) be more specific with the title. Ignoring the challenge though -- great job with the lighting; the backlight and hair halo are really nice as is the looooon shadow.', '2007-10-27 16:56:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199712, 604094, 208, '<td valign="top">Really cool shot. But it doesn''t tell me any story at all about corruption, which is what your title says it is. The distortion is cool, but it''s people who are corrupt, not the building. (And the one burnt out bulb is way too subtle.) This would be great for a feature on restoration or the architecture of City Hall</td>', 'Really cool shot. But it doesn''t tell me any story at all about corruption, which is what your title says it is. The distortion is cool, but it''s people who are corrupt, not the building. (And the one burnt out bulb is way too subtle.) This would be great for a feature on restoration or the architecture of City Hall', '2007-10-27 17:02:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199720, 604173, 208, '<td valign="top">Your title totally makes me think you''ve just shoehorned this otherwise great shot into this challenge. Out of so many other ways to get this in ("Local artist Joe Blow has a vision" "After ten years in prison, innocent man sees freedom") you''ve guaranteed a slew of DNMC votes. I love the framing here - the glasses around the eyes, the hood around the face, and the whole thing off-centered. The b&amp;w really brings the viewer to his face.</td>', 'Your title totally makes me think you''ve just shoehorned this otherwise great shot into this challenge. Out of so many other ways to get this in ("Local artist Joe Blow has a vision" "After ten years in prison, innocent man sees freedom") you''ve guaranteed a slew of DNMC votes. I love the framing here - the glasses around the eyes, the hood around the face, and the whole thing off-centered. The b&w really brings the viewer to his face.', '2007-10-27 17:08:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(4199727, 603847, 84440, '<td valign="top">what takes a simple photograph from boring to sublime? not an easy question and one I am stuggling to understand. This photograph doesn''t tilt toward the sublime. One, it is intended to have sharp focus everywhere but has sharp focus no where. This type of shot needs to be taken from a tripod. The point of view is eye level which brings no special viewpoint. maybe shot right across the water would have been more interesting. The photo balances water, trees, sky but not in a way that is interesting. Cropping off most or all of the sky would at least bring our eyes to the foliage. Try it and see how the foliage becomes more interesting. Puttng the brightest object, the tree out of the water in the center is boring. See how the water at the left is more interesting when there are just limbs coming out of the water. I would guess that you really didn''t try different angles, compositions.</td>', 'what takes a simple photograph from boring to sublime? not an easy question and one I am stuggling to understand. This photograph doesn''t tilt toward the sublime. One, it is intended to have sharp focus everywhere but has sharp focus no where. This type of shot needs to be taken from a tripod. The point of view is eye level which brings no special viewpoint. maybe shot right across the water would have been more interesting. The photo balances water, trees, sky but not in a way that is interesting. Cropping off most or all of the sky would at least bring our eyes to the foliage. Try it and see how the foliage becomes more interesting. Puttng the brightest object, the tree out of the water in the center is boring. See how the water at the left is more interesting when there are just limbs coming out of the water. I would guess that you really didn''t try different angles, compositions.', '2007-10-27 17:17:29.000000', NULL, 1),
