(4215300, 603220, 64929, '<td valign="top">Post-Comments:<br/> <br/>To all the voters that didn''t think this was news worthy enough for the front page, let me fill ya in!  :-)<br/> <br/>This is the construction site of the largest indoor aquatic and recreation center in Northern Arizona!  It happens to be my project site and yes, it appears quite regularly on the front page.  Those columns will support the grand gallery and are quite awesome!  I took this shot on one of my site visits to the construction site and the shadows were incredible that day.....most definitely the shadows of things to come!  <br/> <br/>Sorry it missed - but yeah....very much photojournalism worthy!  :-)<br/> <br/>Thanks, Whiterook, for your support!</td>', 'Post-Comments: To all the voters that didn''t think this was news worthy enough for the front page, let me fill ya in!  :-) This is the construction site of the largest indoor aquatic and recreation center in Northern Arizona!  It happens to be my project site and yes, it appears quite regularly on the front page.  Those columns will support the grand gallery and are quite awesome!  I took this shot on one of my site visits to the construction site and the shadows were incredible that day.....most definitely the shadows of things to come!   Sorry it missed - but yeah....very much photojournalism worthy!  :-) Thanks, Whiterook, for your support!', '2007-11-02 09:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4215510, 603787, 82088, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon and your PB Andrea!  I didn''t vote in this challenge, but from the thumbnails, your photo stood out to me the most.  The picture is very emotive, and I don''t think it is OOF at all, it just looks like heat, which makes the picture that much better IMO.  You can see how hot the ground is right where he is standing, so in response to someone elses comment on the person being anyone is impossible.  Unless you have on the right equipment, you could not be standing where he is standing.  Amazing photo, one to be proud of for sure.</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon and your PB Andrea!  I didn''t vote in this challenge, but from the thumbnails, your photo stood out to me the most.  The picture is very emotive, and I don''t think it is OOF at all, it just looks like heat, which makes the picture that much better IMO.  You can see how hot the ground is right where he is standing, so in response to someone elses comment on the person being anyone is impossible.  Unless you have on the right equipment, you could not be standing where he is standing.  Amazing photo, one to be proud of for sure.', '2007-11-02 10:42:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4215527, 604611, 68947, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot!  I didn''t have time to do any commenting during this challenge, but I have to say that I think this was a great shot.  <br/> <br/>I''m just chuckling here at some of the comments about your exposure and composition. *grin*  My bet is that you were also on the ride in order to have captured this shot, right?  Yeah, I can bet that being whirled around at the same time as your subject, doesn''t exactly lend itself well, to trying to get a shot composed, right lighting, right composition etc.....especially with MINIMAL EDITING!!!! I think it''s terrific that you even caught it in great focus!  <br/> <br/>AND.....since this was a "photojournalism" challenge, this fits very well!  What action shot in the front of newspapers does one see that are perfectly composed and exposed????!!  Peeps are still thinking STOCK SHOTS!!!  *smile*  I wonder how many in here would actually make it as a photojourlist???  "Wait, hold still, gotta compose this shot!  Don''t bring that axe down yet.....haven''t gotten the exposure right yet.  Where''s my light meter?" *wink, grin*<br/> <br/>Nice work!  I think it should have scored MUCH higer......but, then again.....it''s not a fire, is it?! *wink*  <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-02 10:53:29.</i></td>', 'I really like this shot!  I didn''t have time to do any commenting during this challenge, but I have to say that I think this was a great shot.   I''m just chuckling here at some of the comments about your exposure and composition. *grin*  My bet is that you were also on the ride in order to have captured this shot, right?  Yeah, I can bet that being whirled around at the same time as your subject, doesn''t exactly lend itself well, to trying to get a shot composed, right lighting, right composition etc.....especially with MINIMAL EDITING!!!! I think it''s terrific that you even caught it in great focus!   AND.....since this was a "photojournalism" challenge, this fits very well!  What action shot in the front of newspapers does one see that are perfectly composed and exposed????!!  Peeps are still thinking STOCK SHOTS!!!  *smile*  I wonder how many in here would actually make it as a photojourlist???  "Wait, hold still, gotta compose this shot!  Don''t bring that axe down yet.....haven''t gotten the exposure right yet.  Where''s my light meter?" *wink, grin* Nice work!  I think it should have scored MUCH higer......but, then again.....it''s not a fire, is it?! *wink*  ', '2007-11-02 10:50:51.000000', '2007-11-02 10:53:29.000000', 0),
