(4215927, 604642, 24454, '<td valign="top">Cory, THANK YOU for sharing this photo!!!   My heart is so burdened for our troops over there. . .especially the ones I know and care for like you and Deb . . .so to see something like this. . .play.  fun.  Taken so well.  It just makes my day and heals my heart! <br/> <br/>I wish it scored right at the top. . .but it is just a wonderful photo no matter where it placed!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Cory, THANK YOU for sharing this photo!!!   My heart is so burdened for our troops over there. . .especially the ones I know and care for like you and Deb . . .so to see something like this. . .play.  fun.  Taken so well.  It just makes my day and heals my heart!  I wish it scored right at the top. . .but it is just a wonderful photo no matter where it placed!! ', '2007-11-02 14:07:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4216138, 603787, 52549, '<td valign="top">What a terrific score and what a terrific image. Perfect for the challenge and a well deserved blue. Many congratulations.</td>', 'What a terrific score and what a terrific image. Perfect for the challenge and a well deserved blue. Many congratulations.', '2007-11-02 15:27:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4216152, 604387, 52549, '<td valign="top">This is one of the most moving and powerful images I''ve seen. A most excellent image. Congratulations on your red ribbon, Brad.</td>', 'This is one of the most moving and powerful images I''ve seen. A most excellent image. Congratulations on your red ribbon, Brad.', '2007-11-02 15:30:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4216156, 604358, 52549, '<td valign="top">Awesome capture, good work. Big congrats on 3rd place.</td>', 'Awesome capture, good work. Big congrats on 3rd place.', '2007-11-02 15:32:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4216159, 602939, 52549, '<td valign="top">I''m pleased your shot did so well, Skip. Photojournalism at its finest!</td>', 'I''m pleased your shot did so well, Skip. Photojournalism at its finest!', '2007-11-02 15:33:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4216197, 602453, 68035, '<td valign="top">I agree that the world would be a better place if papers focussed as much on good news as they did on bad news.  I thought this was a lovely action shot of kids just having fun<br/> <br/>One thing I would say though is the league may not keep the scores, but I bet the kids and parents do!!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-02 15:47:54.</i></td>', 'I agree that the world would be a better place if papers focussed as much on good news as they did on bad news.  I thought this was a lovely action shot of kids just having fun One thing I would say though is the league may not keep the scores, but I bet the kids and parents do!!!', '2007-11-02 15:47:15.000000', '2007-11-02 15:47:54.000000', 0),
(4216233, 604187, 1031, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments -- I thought this did surprisingly well!<br/> <br/>I had taken a tighter-in shot as a couple people suggested, but I really wanted to show the broad expansiveness of the memorial/protest more than focus on the individual markers -- I figured as long as the figures on the sign were legible it would work.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=607680" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/607680.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/607680.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/607680.jpg"/></a> <br/>I did try making it grayscale, but it was just too tonally flat to use without editing not permitted in this challenge. Also in a "real" photojournalistic situation, I''d have probably cropped out the road and part of the sky as was suggested.<br/> <br/>My camera doesn''t have a very wide-angle setting; what I really would have wanted is more like this panoramic, stitched from six hand-held shots using Autostitch.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=607209" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/607209.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/607209.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/0-4999/1031/120/607209.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments -- I thought this did surprisingly well! I had taken a tighter-in shot as a couple people suggested, but I really wanted to show the broad expansiveness of the memorial/protest more than focus on the individual markers -- I figured as long as the figures on the sign were legible it would work. I did try making it grayscale, but it was just too tonally flat to use without editing not permitted in this challenge. Also in a "real" photojournalistic situation, I''d have probably cropped out the road and part of the sky as was suggested. My camera doesn''t have a very wide-angle setting; what I really would have wanted is more like this panoramic, stitched from six hand-held shots using Autostitch.', '2007-11-02 16:03:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4216273, 602939, 16739, '<td valign="top">dude great shot ,</td>', 'dude great shot ,', '2007-11-02 16:30:51.000000', NULL, 0),
